    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336-a1">

                <pb facs="0460" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg450"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-26">January 26,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Memorandum for H. M. Jr.</p>
                <p>I still think that this can be worked out as soon as Fox gets here. If they don’t
                    want dollar notes, why don’t we buy Chinese yuans and use them for paying for
                    the equipment of Chinese troops in China itself. I would be wholly willing to go
                    up to twenty or twenty-five million dollars a month on some such basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
